ssignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2021-04-22T09:00:56Z","updated_at":"2022-02-01T22:58:54Z","closed_at":"2022-02-01T22:58:54Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Function _collide_ in _collide_aabb_ misses to detect a collision if the two objects are intersecting but not by a side.\r\nMaybe is my idea of collision but the two following objects should be detected as colliding:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlet a_pos = Vec3::new(8.0, 0.0, 0.0);\r\n\r\nlet a_size = Vec2::new(10.0, 10.0);\r\n\r\nlet b_pos = Vec3::new(8.0, 0.0, 0.0);\r\nlet b_size = Vec2::new(6.0, 100.0);\r\n\r\nlet collision = collide(a_pos, a_size, b_pos, b_size);\r\nprintln!(\"collision {:?}\", collision); // ... I expect to have a collision here\r\n```\r\nIt's more evident if we check the behavior on moving objects:\r\n\r\n``` \r\nlet mut a_pos = Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 0.0);\r\nlet a_size = Vec2::new(10.0, 10.0);\r\n\r\nlet b_pos = Vec3::new(8.0, 0.0, 0.0);\r\nlet b_size = Vec2::new(6.0, 100.0);\r\n\r\nloop {\t\r\n\tlet collision = collide(a_pos, a_size, b_pos, b_size);\r\n\tprintln!(\"a_pos.x {:?} => collision {:?}\", a_pos.x, collision);\r\n\ta_pos.x += 1.0;\r\n\tif a_pos.x > 16.0 {\r\n\t\tbreak;\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThe problem is the heuristics to determine the side of collision.\r\nAn easy solution is to add a generic Collision::Intersecting collision.\r\n\r\nI attach my proposed patch here (with tests)\r\n[collide_aabb.patch.txt](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/files/6356914/collide_aabb.patch.txt)\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"bors[bot]","id":26634292,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjY2MzQyOTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bors%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/bors","followers_url":"https://api.g